The previous system design was this: ./assets/system-design.png

It consisted of:

- 1 Gateway (NGinx) that would load balance between 3 instances of the server (App)  
- 3 instances of the server (App) that would process requests  
- 1 instance of a health check service (Doctor) that would check the status of each Payments service  
- 1 instance of Payments (Default) that would process payments  
- 1 instance of Payments (Fallback) that would only process when Payments (Default) failed  

However, I noticed these problems:

1. If both Payments services failed, the entire system would stop.  
2. If the App received a message from the Doctor saying that Payments was down, it wouldn’t update the state variable in time, causing the App to lose the current request.  
3. The App would be doing more than one thing at once (receiving requests, listening for Doctor updates, sending status to Doctor, and sending requests to Payments).  
4. The App wasn’t counting how many requests each Payments instance had received, which is one of the prerequisites.  

So, I came up with the new system design strategy:

